<!-- SWITCHING FROM COMPETITORS -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="display:inline-flex;">Switching From a Specific Platform?</div>
      <h2>What changes when you move to TurnCom360</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="switch-grid">
      <div class="switch-card">
        <h3>Switching from RingCentral?</h3>
        <p>RingCentral is built for enterprise self-management. You configure, you troubleshoot, you manage users. TurnCom360 manages it for you. You lose the configuration portal (you won&rsquo;t miss it). You gain a team that answers when something goes wrong.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="switch-card">
        <h3>Switching from Ooma?</h3>
        <p>Ooma is priced for 1&ndash;2 phone setups. When you&rsquo;ve grown past that, the per-user pricing and feature gaps start to hurt. TurnCom360&rsquo;s flat monthly plan typically runs better value above 5 users, with more routing capability and actual pre-programming included.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="switch-card">
        <h3>Switching from Vonage?</h3>
        <p>Vonage&rsquo;s contract structure and hidden fees are our most common complaint from switchers. If you&rsquo;re mid-contract, we&rsquo;ll help you map the best exit. Once you&rsquo;re free, month-to-month from day one &mdash; no more multi-year trap.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="switch-card">
        <h3>Switching from a legacy PBX?</h3>
        <p>Older on-premise PBX systems require expensive hardware maintenance and in-house technicians. Moving to TurnCom360 cloud VoIP eliminates the hardware and the headcount. Your calls move to our infrastructure &mdash; no servers, no maintenance contracts.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


